From 76c5e51f2431ebb949b1805f599c7f0950bdcf5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] test-posix: Check <sys/resource.h>, and setrlimit in
 children

test-setrlimit lowered every limit of its own process and failed when
a hard limit was below 2, as RLIMIT_CORE can be. Make the changes in a
child for each resource, skip those whose hard limit is below 2, and
check EPERM, EINVAL and that RLIM_INFINITY is the largest value. Check
that the limits are enforced and kept across exec, the
<sys/resource.h> declarations, and that the XSI functions are hidden in
strict mode. test-setrlimit now skips without processes, so the CMake
build runs it too.
